  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal monatomic gas undergoes a cyclic process as shown in the figure. If the temperature of the gas at state <math><mn>1</mn></math> is <math><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and at state <math><mn>4</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, then heat exchanged during process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>→</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0069_5af95a415b59.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 129px;\" />"
  },
